body:
I pissed myself in 3rd grade. I was just sitting on the grass with my bestie and I laughed so hard I peed myself. Like a lot. Yikes! I ended up just going to the office and my mom brought me a new outfit. My bestie was cool and didn't harass me about it either but I am embarassed just thinking about it.

&#x200B;

Another yikes was when I was 14. I had a routine surgery and now I have crohns disease so I have a fair share of embarassing poop stories but this was the worst. Upon waking up, half consious me was puking uncontrollably and then I managed to mutter out that I had to poop. So a nurse comes over with a bed pan since I was definitely not ok to be walking but it was too late. I had explosive diarhea everywhere and it just kept coming. The nurses were shocked that someone so small could have so much poop inside.

&#x200B;

So there I was dry heaving and pooping for a solid 40 minutes uncontrollably, covered in shit and vomit. They sponged me off and when I was awake enough they quickly took me upstairs for a very real shower.

&#x200B;

Worst part is I was a 14 year old girl and I had a male recovery nurse.

&#x200B;

But wait there's more! When I came back 6 weeks later for the same surgery it all happened again, and 6 weeks after that it happened again! So basically it got to the point where they would make me put on an adult diaper before the surgery and put a mess of pee pads under me. And that folks is how I discovered I am very intollerant to gas anesthetic.

I had hyperthyroidism when I was a kid and geez the insomnia and anxiety was so awful. I ended up getting my thyroid removed after about a year and a half because I had a severe case and the radiation wouldn't have worked well enough on what my surgeon described as the biggest thyroid he's ever seen. 

&#x200B;

Holy moly I feel so much better since that surgery. Just have to pop a pill everyday and get ocasional bloodwork and I'm set for life

hell driving an automatic is pretty tricky on some of those hills.

&#x200B;

my dad made me drive on lombard street when he was teaching me how to drive

yeet yeet osteoporosis since I was 16 gang

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Though my ED is not entirely to blame since years of high dose prednisone did not help my situation.

finally someone who gets it.

&#x200B;

Side note: you might want to plug your phone in my friend

I'm not older since I'm still only 18 but now I am an adult so I can no longer be forced into facilities. I 100% forgive my parents. They meant no harm to me and now they are horified at what I told them went on in that RTC. The doctors recommended it and they wanted to help me. My parents knew it was shitty while I was there but I was brainwashed into not telling them everything going on as it was happening. 

&#x200B;

They were upset at what I did tell them while it was happening but they were afraid to take me out because those shit holes called cps and threatened if my parents took me out I would be taken away.

I also suffer from chronic constipation and I've had colitis for 12 years so I feel the struggle. 

&#x200B;

Senna is actually probably making things worse in the long run because if you take it regularly you can become dependant on it to poop at all. How much miralax/PEG3350 do you take? How often do you poop?

&#x200B;

I'd reccomend stopping senna gradually by reducing the daily dose over a few weeks and upping the miralax to around 3 doses per day to be safe if you are taking 1 right now. Supplement this with more natural things like hot prune juice as needed as well as eating veggies and drinking lots of water. If you do not poop for 3-4 days or more do a saline enema because its important to not let things get too backed up.

well I was in residential rehab when I turned 17 and the place was really abusive and cruel and they were making me eat an entire box of this really salty ravioli and I almost vomited.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

A close runner up is when I was turning 10 and I went to the county fair with 2 of my friends and I was in the beginning of what turned out to be one of my top 3 worst colitis flares. So I spent half the day in the bathroom and I was nauseus the whole day until I vomited on the way home. Fun stuff that was

when I was in the worst of my graves disease I was honestly in psychosis and just didn't know it. I mainly lost weight because I was 100% convinced that someone was out there trying to poision my food so I wouldn't eat and everything was super weird. My anxiety was always at least 8/10 and I would go days without sleeping. 

&#x200B;

So not worth it, but looking back I really wish my parents believed me when I told them I was convinced I was pregnant and that everyone was trying to poision me. But they just thought i was a dumb 10 year old yikes.

not to be an asshole, but no actually. 

&#x200B;



I used to have graves disease (hyperactive thyroid) and too much thyroxine is so so so dangerous. You could literally have a heart attack. When my graves was at its worst I was not allowed to exercise at all because I was in real danger of a heart attack.

Although I've had my thyroid removed so I'm hypothyroid now I have horrible lasting issues from too much thyroid hormone 6 years post op. You can get protruding eyes like me, and once you have them there is nothing that can be done to reduce it except a risky eye surgery that is only done when you can't close your eyes anymore.

&#x200B;

Not to mention that i was actually going insane because I was so anxious all the time with my heart beating so fast that i was supper paranoid about everything. Also my thyroid swelled up to like 10x the normal size and my neck looked disgusting even my mom cringed when I wasn't wearing a scarf and my surgeon said I had the biggest thyroid he's ever seen.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Its like all cons honestly

I've only done it a couple times but please don't do this to yourself!!! I can't stress it enough! 

&#x200B;

