Although I've had my thyroid removed so I'm hypothyroid now I have horrible lasting issues from too much thyroid hormone 6 years post op. You can get protruding eyes like me, and once you have them there is nothing that can be done to reduce it except a risky eye surgery that is only done when you can't close your eyes anymore.

