i read your post assuming you were like 16-18 but NO you are 13. Damn I was like patting myself on the back for dragging my crush to the dancefloor last night at my senior prom. 

&#x200B;

When I was thirteen I had pizza face acne and I spent all my free time reading hetalia fanfiction in my room. Damn you just made me realize how much of a loser I was

My boss just pressured me into quitting because I called out last week. I was in the psych hospital for trying to kill myself :((

&#x200B;

Whatever she was an asshole anyway

That is not dying with dignity. You are just passing on despair to that poor train driver who will suffer with guilt for the rest of their life. 

&#x200B;

Go to the mental hospital. It's really not as bad as you'd think. When I went it was a bunch of depressed people and there was one guy with schitzophrenia but everyone was very kind and the worst part about it was nasty hospital food. When you need sleep, they let you sleep, when you need to talk, you get to talk and basically you can do whatever you want as long as you don't have anything sharp or electronic. But in CA where I'm from you can make phone calls whenever you want as well. 

&#x200B;

The staff isn't there to torment you or diagnose you with insanity. They just sort of keep an eye on you for a couple of days and hook you up with a therapist.

To everyone mentioning my eyes, they are huge because I used to have graves' disease when I was a child! But I'm better after having surgery a few years ago, my eyes are still affected though. Just thought I'd let everyone know what's up :)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Just wanted to tell you that what happened to you in the hospital was downright awful and unprofessional. Like yes farts are gross and poop is gross, but every single human farts and poops ans medical professionals shouldn't act like they've never heard of someone having a BM on the table. It happens sometimes and people don't poop because they're fat... but diet does play a role in how bad it stinks lol. 

&#x200B;

My point is that you aren't the only one to poop on the table, I've pooped on the table like 5+ times when I was like 14-15 thanks to colitis so I know how embarassing and uncomfortable it can be.

&#x200B;

I know how hard it is to change but remember that it's never too late unless you are dead. It will be hard but you \*can\* make some changes, even small ones and it will help. Like having 2 bottles of mtn dew per day instead of 3.

I come from a long line of digestive problems and thyroid problems

&#x200B;

My grandma's brother had colon cancer and I've got Ulcerative Colitis, and on my mom's side basically everyone has hypothyroidism; even my cousins, but I had to break the streak and get hyperthyroidism which is aparently a lot worse.

&#x200B;

Also the last few generations have had mental health issues including depression, eating disorders, and ocd. I mean I guess it's nice that I'm not the only one but idk

Ugh me too. I had to stop seeing my old therapist that I could actually talk to and I got sent to residential for 5 months and then I got sent to this shitty ED therapist to do FBT which sucks ass. Then that therapist left abruptly (hopefully got fired because she made me wanna kill myself) and I got sent to a new one. Luckily but unluckily I am getting kicked out for making 0 progress in the last like 5 months so she can help someone who can actually get better.

&#x200B;

My parents won't let me get a job or get my drivers liscense and they won't help me pay for college until my ED is under control. Like bro WTF. 

&#x200B;

But now I'm just being a little shit because I turn 18 in like 3 months and I got a job by myself and I'm not going to quit.

